---
// The open source build page at https://openact.ing/build: build your own custom apps on the free OpenAct core.
// Its Producer twin is producer.astro. Both share the "What you could build" section (components/build/Ideas.astro).
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import "../styles/home.css";
import "../styles/build.css";
import Ideas from "../components/build/Ideas.astro";
import { DEMO_URL, DEPLOY_URL, DOCS_URL } from "../site";
---
<Site
  path="/build"
  title="Build your own apps on OpenAct"
  description="Build custom agentic apps for your business on the free, open source OpenAct core. A coding agent builds the app. You own the code and the data."
  ogTitle="Build your first app on OpenAct"
  ogDescription="Describe the app. Your coding agent builds it on the free OpenAct core. You own the code and the data."
>
  <div class="wrap hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source · Build it yourself</p>
      <h1>Build the app<br /><em>your business needs.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">Describe the app in plain words. A coding agent such as Claude Code or Codex builds it on the OpenAct core. Sign-in, companies, roles, email and agents are ready. You own the code and the data.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href={DEPLOY_URL}>Deploy to Cloudflare</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost arrow" href={`${DOCS_URL}/apps`}>Read the app guide</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Free under the Apache License 2.0. Runs in your own Cloudflare account.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-key">
      <div class="card terminal" aria-label="Ask a coding agent to build an OpenAct app">
        <div class="head"><span>~/openact</span><i></i></div>
        <pre><span class="p">&gt;</span> Build a client intake app. A lead fills in
  a form. The agent drafts a scope and a price.
  A person approves it before it goes out.
<span class="c">  reading AGENTS.md · docs/apps.md
  writing apps/intake · tests pass</span>
<span class="p">$</span> npm run deploy
<span class="c">  migrations applied · worker live</span>
<span class="p">$</span> <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></pre>
        <div class="done">
          <span class="chip ok">Intake · on</span>
          <span class="chip ok">Projects · on</span>
          <span class="chip">your account</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 id="how-title">From an idea to a live app.</h2>
        <p>You do not start from zero. The core does the hard parts. Your app adds only its own features.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bento">
        <article class="card s4 phase">
          <p class="num">01</p>
          <p class="tag">Step 1 · Deploy</p>
          <h3>Put OpenAct on your account.</h3>
          <p>Deploy the free core to your own Cloudflare account with one click. Projects comes with it.</p>
          <div class="out"><p><b>Outcome:</b> your own OpenAct site, with sign-in and companies ready.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card s4 phase">
          <p class="num">02</p>
          <p class="tag">Step 2 · Describe</p>
          <h3>Tell your agent what to build.</h3>
          <p>Describe the app to Claude Code or Codex. The agent follows the rules in AGENTS.md, the Promptbook and the shared components.</p>
          <div class="out"><p><b>Outcome:</b> a working app in its own folder, with tests.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="card s4 phase">
          <p class="num">03</p>
          <p class="tag">Step 3 · Ship</p>
          <h3>Deploy and use it.</h3>
          <p>Run one deploy command. The app shows in the app rail for each company that turns it on.</p>
          <div class="out"><p><b>Outcome:</b> a live app that your team uses, on your account.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="core" aria-labelledby="core-title">
      <div class="card split">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why build on OpenAct</p>
          <h3 id="core-title">Your agent builds on a stage that is already set.</h3>
          <p>A coding agent can write an app fast. The hard part is everything around it: sign-in, access, data that stays apart and agents with limits.</p>
          <p>OpenAct gives your agent all of that, plus clear rules to follow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="points">
          <div class="key"><strong>Ready on day one</strong><span>Sign-in, companies, roles, email, files and the app shell.</span></div>
          <div class="key"><strong>Rules for coding agents</strong><span>AGENTS.md, the app guide and the Promptbook tell the agent how to build.</span></div>
          <div class="key"><strong>Agents with limits</strong><span>An app agent never does more than the person's role allows. Risky steps wait for approval.</span></div>
          <div class="key"><strong>Your account, your data</strong><span>It runs on Cloudflare Workers, D1 and R2 in your own account.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Ideas mode="diy" />

    <section class="card cross" aria-labelledby="cross-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow warm">Producer plan</p>
        <h3 id="cross-title">Want us to build it with you?</h3>
        <p>Producer is our done-for-you studio. We run OpenAct and build your primary custom app with you.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost arrow" href="/producer">See Producer</a>
    </section>

    <section class="card closer" aria-labelledby="closer-title">
      <div class="closer-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Your turn</p>
          <h2 id="closer-title">Take the stage.</h2>
          <p>Custom software is not only for engineers now. Deploy the free core, and build your first app this week.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="start">
          <div class="key"><b>01</b>Deploy OpenAct to Cloudflare.</div>
          <div class="key"><b>02</b>Describe your app to a coding agent.</div>
          <div class="key"><b>03</b>Deploy it and invite your team.</div>
          <a class="btn btn-accent" href={DEPLOY_URL}>Deploy to Cloudflare</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={DEMO_URL}>Try the demo first</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Site>
